// @ARGS: --lib tests/lib
// @falsified-by: tests/falsified/c98-a-name-kept-below-a-facade-names-the-library-that-kept-it.patch — interpret exit 1 -> 0, interpret expectations FAIL/1 -> 0/1 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches), native exit 1 -> 0, native expectations FAIL/1 -> 0/1 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches)
//   CHANNEL: the compile error's TEXT — the file is refused on both trees, and the
//   expectation matches only where the error names `c98_private` and `c98_math`.
//   WITNESS: the control says `Unknown function c98_unit` and nothing more.
//   HOLDS: the program is refused on both trees with exactly one error; no assert runs
//   and nothing leaks or panics on either.
//
// @C98 — the name stops one library further down than the program looks: `c98_outer`
// passes `c98_private` on, and `c98_private` imports `c98_math` with a plain `use`, which
// serves its own file only.  The error names the library that kept the name, found
// through the facade, rather than a bare "Unknown function" that leaves the author to
// search every module for it (met in moros: `hex_to_world` kept by `moros_sim`'s
// `player` module, reported as unknown with no hint).
use c98_outer::*;

// @EXPECT_ERROR: `c98_private` uses it from `c98_math` but does not pass it on
fn test_a_name_kept_below_a_facade() {
  assert(c98_unit() == 1, "unreached");
}
